From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ps4-gladius <ps4-gladius@invalid>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 10:10:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: survive a NULL environ.

The client and the in-process server now complete their handshake --

    WINE wine startup: server connected

-- and start_main_thread carries on to get_initial_environment, which faults at
address 0:

    PW_WINE64 fault signal=0xb addr=0x0 rip=0x800884612   (env.c:877)

    for (e = environ; *e; e++) *size += strlen(*e) + 6;

environ is NULL. A title inherits no environment, and this module's libc leaves
the list NULL until something writes to it -- pw_ps4_setenv, which the title
calls through the module's descriptor, because each module otherwise carries a
private one. Wine takes POSIX at its word and dereferences it unguarded.

Carry on with an empty environment instead of dying, and say so once through
klog. This is not the whole story: an empty environment means no WINEPREFIX and
no HOME, so Wine will go looking for its prefix somewhere else. The title's own
"environment status=0" covers only its setenv and never the module's, so
pw_prx_env_ps4.c now reports what reached this environ -- "never called" and
"called and did not take" have looked identical until now.
---
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/env.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/env.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/env.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/env.c
@@ -872,14 +872,28 @@ static WCHAR *get_initial_environment( SIZE_T *pos, SIZE_T *size )
     char **e;
     WCHAR *env, *ptr, *end;
 
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+    /* ⚠ A title has no environment to inherit, and this module's libc leaves
+     * environ NULL until something writes to it (pw_ps4_setenv, which the title
+     * calls through the module's descriptor). Wine assumes POSIX gives it a
+     * list and walked straight into the NULL here, faulting at address 0 with
+     * the whole client/server handshake already behind it. Say so and carry on
+     * with an empty environment rather than die. */
+    if (!environ)
+    {
+        extern int sceKernelDebugOutText( int channel, const char *text );
+        sceKernelDebugOutText( 0, "wine: environ is NULL; starting with an empty environment\n" );
+    }
+#endif
+
     /* estimate needed size */
     *size = 1;
-    for (e = environ; *e; e++) *size += strlen(*e) + 6;
+    for (e = environ; e && *e; e++) *size += strlen(*e) + 6;
 
     env = malloc( *size * sizeof(WCHAR) );
     ptr = env;
     end = env + *size - 1;
-    for (e = environ; *e && ptr < end; e++)
+    for (e = environ; e && *e && ptr < end; e++)
     {
         char *str = *e;
 
-- 
